[2026-04-11 17:13:42] LLM OUTPUT: Thought: I will write a Python script named drone_chase_simulation.py that simulates two drones: a target drone moving in a simple pattern and a chaser drone that moves towards the target. The script will print their positions each step and stop when the chaser intercepts the target.

Action: FILE_WRITE
Action Input: {"path":"drone_chase_simulation.py","content":"import math\nimport time\n\nclass Drone:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, speed):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.speed = speed\n\n    def position(self):\n        return (self.x, self.y)\n\n    def move_towards(self, target_x, target_y):\n        dx = target_x - self.x\n        dy = target_y - self.y\n        distance = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n        if distance == 0:\n            return\n        step = min(self.speed, distance)\n        self.x += step * dx / distance\n        self.y += step * dy / distance\n\n    def move_in_pattern(self, step_count):\n        # Simple pattern: move right and up alternately\n        if step_count % 2 == 0:\n            self.x += self.speed\n        else:\n            self.y += self.speed\n\n\ndef distance(d1, d2):\n    return math.hypot(d1.x - d2.x, d1.y - d2.y)\n\n\ndef main():\n    target = Drone(0, 0, 1.0)  # Target drone\n    chaser = Drone(-10, -10, 1.5)  # Chaser drone\n\n    step_count = 0\n    while True:\n        target.move_in_pattern(step_count)\n        chaser.move_towards(target.x, target.y)\n\n        print(f\"Step {step_count}: Target at {target.position()}, Chaser at {chaser.position()}\")\n\n        if distance(target, chaser) < 0.1:\n            print(\"Chaser has intercepted the target!\")\n            break\n\n        step_count += 1\n        time.sleep(0.1)  # Slow down the simulation for readability\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}
